WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:04.100
-Our first guest tonight is an
Emmy- and Tony-nominated actor

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.801
you know from the hit series
"Stranger Things"

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:08.067
and movies like "Black Widow"
and "Violent Night."

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:09.701
He stars in "We Have a Ghost,"

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.701
which premieres
February 24th on Netflix.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:13.567
Please welcome back to the show
our friend David Harbour,

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.767
everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.934
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:24.334
♪♪

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:30.701
♪♪

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:33.667
Welcome back!
-Whoa! Wow, what a crowd.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.100
-We're always
so happy you're here.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.634
-What a crowd.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:38.868
-We were talking backstage,
you were here

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.434
for when we were in the studio
with no crowds.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.767
-Yeah, that was dark times.
-That was dark times.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:46.000
-Just like five producers
enthusiastically clapping

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.634
like a child's ballet recital.
Like, "Oh, my God,

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.667
you're doing so great!"
-Yeah.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:53.567
-I will say,
after those 12 months,

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.534
I'm like,
"I'm a very fancy boy."

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:57.901
[ Laughter ]
I fell for it.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:01:00.367
They convinced me.
-You're not wrong.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:02.601
-Oh, thank you very much.
I want to start with something,

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:03.968
I'm just gonna
get it out of the way.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.567
You and your wife, the
incredibly talented Lily Allen,

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.767
you gave a tour
to "Architectural Digest"...

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.334
-[ Chuckles ]
-...of your home.

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:15.133
And it became a lot of -- it
sort of entered the discourse.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.100
People wanted to talk
about your apartment,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.033
including the fact that you have
a carpeted bathroom.

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:20.400
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.234
[ Laughter ]
-Listen to the groaning already.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:26.234
We're gonna talk about this.
-Okay.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.667
So, what was this -- Was this
a couple's decision?

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.667
Did you both feel strongly
about a carpeted bathroom?

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.067
-No.
-Okay.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:34.334
-I made very few decisions
in this house.

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:36.601
-Gotcha.
How do you feel about it so far?

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:40.033
-Look, I like it.
[ Laughter ].

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:46.167
There's a romance
to a carpeted bathroom.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.501
-Uh-huh.
-You know what I mean?

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:50.434
-Because you feel like?
-Well, like you're in Paris

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:53.801
in the '20s.
-Before they invented tiles?

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.734
-Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:59.734
-Smoking Gitanes and
inhaling black mold.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:02.033
-Yeah. Oh, right.
This is an era

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:03.601
before people knew
that was a bad thing,

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:06.033
where they would just
squish out of the tub

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:08.667
and just leave.
-Yeah, you just roll out.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.534
Get those wet feet
all over there

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.767
for years and years and just --

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:14.634
whatever accumulates,
accumulates.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.167
I like terrariums.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:22.067
It did seem like social media
fell, like, very hardly

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.000
on the side of
"This is not okay."

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.033
-I think everybody has become
such a nerd after COVID.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:29.701
You know what I mean?
-Yeah.

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:33.167
-We're so -- such squares.
It's like, whatever.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:36.334
A little bit of, you know, mold.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.334 --> 00:02:39.667
-Some might argue
it fights the COVID, right?

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:41.100
[ Laughter ]
Like, if you have enough --

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.868
COVID looks at a house like this
and is like, "No, thank you."

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:46.467
[ Laughter ].

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.133
-But we pulled some tweets.

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:49.501
You've not seen
these tweets yet.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.501
-I have not seen these.
Oh, my God.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:52.901
-Here you go.
Do you want to just read it?

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.601
-Yeah. I'm sorry.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:57.968
"I just watched
the David Harbour/Lily Allen

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.667
A.D. house story.
Carpet in the bathroom

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:02.367
should be
a cancellable offense."

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.934
-I do like --
-I guess that's bad

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:08.100
for the promotion of my movie.
Yeah, that's...

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:14.100
-From Prill, "What the [Bleep]
do Lily Allen and David Harbour

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.601
have a carpeted bathroom?"
"Why? Why the [Bleep]."

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.300
-Yeah.
And then this is nice

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.334
because this is obviously
a fan of yours.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.601
-"Not even David Harbour
can make me feel good

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:26.133
about carpet in the bathroom."
[ Laughter ].

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:29.501
[ Applause ]
-I don't know. I like it.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:33.901
I like everything about it.
Now, you referred to this --

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.100
-Keeping this one.
-Okay, good.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.734
You referred to this
as a space fridge.

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:38.934
-Yeah.
We got to talk about this.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:40.667
-Okay, so, you called it
a space fridge.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.834
People got even angrier
'cause then they were like,

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:45.334
"You got a fridge
in your bathroom?"

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:47.133
[ Laughter ]
-It's not a fridge.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:49.534
-Okay.
-It's not an actual fridge.

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:51.501
-Okay.
-It just looks like

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.534
a fridge from space.
-Got it.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:56.033
-Like a NASA fridge.
-So it's like a cabinet.

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:58.100
-It's a cabinet where you put,
like, lotions in

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.067
and things like that.
-But you guys wanted,

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:03.501
in that same sort of
theme of romance,

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:05.634
you wanted to feel like
a fridge was in your bathroom.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.701
[ Laughter ]
-Like a fridge from outer space.

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:10.234
Like romance. You know, romance.
-You want it to be like

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:13.367
you were both in 1920s France
and way in the future.

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.901
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly. It's like "Star Wars."

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:19.501
"A long, long time ago
in a galaxy far away."

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:22.200
-So, that far back.
-We carpet bathrooms,

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.033
and we keep our products
in a space fridge.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.834
-You know what? You guys --
-You get us.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:28.567
-I get you so much.
-I love it!

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.701
-Now I want to ask
if your kids get you.

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.400
They're at the age
where they're opinionated,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:34.334
you were telling me backstage,
10 and 11.

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:35.901
What do they think
about the design?

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:39.234
-They've described it as --
they said,

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:40.834
"Mommy, we live
in a clown house."

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:42.667
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:45.667
-It's not that bad.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:48.267
I mean, there's got to be
places for clowns...

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:49.667
-Yeah.
-...in this world.

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.467
-Right, you can't just expect
them to all live in a car.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:57.234
-Yeah, they don't like that.
-Are you strict with the kids?

00:04:57.234 --> 00:05:01.634
-I mean, I go through phases.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.167
-Uh-huh.
-It's getting harder, I think,

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:07.133
that they're getting
smarter and older.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.334
It's easier to be strict

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:12.167
when they're younger
and sort of dumber.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:14.267
[ Laughter ]
I had a -- This was --

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:17.133
I had an experience where --
it was during the pandemic --

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.734
one of them had thrown out
a piece of paper

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:22.167
that was really important.
It was some kind of something.

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:23.801
I don't know.
But it was the whole day

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:25.601
we spent looking
for this piece of paper.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:28.033
And finally, we found it
in the trash can.

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.467
One of them had thrown it out,

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:31.467
and neither of them
would fess up to it.

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:36.901
And we were furious.
And I said, I am gonna find out

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:39.400
who threw this thing out."

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.467
And I brought in
a dish of flour.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.634 --> 00:05:47.300
And I had them
dip their fingers in it.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:51.501
And I just went away, silent.
I went away.

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:54.133
Put it down, I came back,
and I said, "Listen,

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:57.434
I know how
to fingerprint people."

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:59.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.601 --> 00:06:01.868
"Because I've done
a lot of cop shows."

00:06:01.868 --> 00:06:05.634
[ Laughter ]
It's true.

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:07.234
What I didn't realize
at the time was

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:09.767
that you're supposed to actually
put their fingers in ink.

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.467
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:13.400
You did some of
the lesser cop shows.

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.033
-You're supposed to dust
for the print.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:17.501
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-I didn't do that.

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:19.434
-You did it backwards.
-I did it backwards.

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:22.067
[ Laughter ]
But they still believed me.

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:25.567
I left, and I came back
with a little piece of paper.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:28.634
And I said, "I have the results
of the fingerprinting."

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:29.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.968 --> 00:06:33.067
"So if you'd like to tell me
now who actually did it,

00:06:33.067 --> 00:06:35.434
it'll be easier for you."
-Wow.

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:36.868
-Yeah.
-Did it work?

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:38.300
-It worked like a charm.
-Wow!

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:39.801
-Yeah, they immediately
fessed up.

00:06:39.801 --> 00:06:42.467
[ Applause ]
Thank you! Thank you.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:45.200
-You won them back after the old
carpet in the bathroom.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.934
-[ Laughs ]
Once they get to be like 11,

00:06:47.934 --> 00:06:49.901
though, they just think
you're an idiot

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.467
for doing things like that,
which you are.

00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:54.501
-Yeah, yeah.
Trying to get an 11-year-old

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:56.467
to put your fingers in flour,
good luck.

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:58.400
[ Laughter ]
"Get out of here, old man."

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.601
They just blow it back
in your face.

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:02.868
-"I've done a lot of cop shows."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.868 --> 00:07:05.000
-I want to ask
about your new movie.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.801
We'll be right back
with more from David Harbour.

